WEBVTT

00:00:00.320 --> 00:01:35.400
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

00:01:35.930 --> 00:01:39.770
[Abyss]

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:10.860
[Episode 3]

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.520
I found this novel online.

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:15.300
Zhao Ganzhe asked the technicians
to check,

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.030
[Dingdian Novel Website]

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.480
[Abyss; Chapter 6] [Han Sheng]

00:03:17.579 --> 00:03:18.900
and they confirmed
that the author of the novel

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:19.750
[Abyss; Chapter 6] [Han Sheng]

00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:20.670
is Han Pinmu.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.579
"Zhou Li hesitated
outside the warehouse door.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:27.190
From inside came muffled, agonized sobs."

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:28.829
Come meet me at Fan's Canteen.

00:03:28.829 --> 00:03:30.000
[Sender: Old Foodie]

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:31.440
[Come meet me at Fan's Canteen.]

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:38.180
Smell it, smell it.

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:39.620
Take in that wok hei.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.660
Smells so good.

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:46.250
Here you go.

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:54.410
So tender.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:56.360
Come on, try some. Come on.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.079
Really. It tastes so good.

00:03:58.930 --> 00:03:59.710
Try it.

00:03:59.710 --> 00:04:00.840
Just this one plate?

00:04:01.030 --> 00:04:01.760
It's enough.

00:04:02.650 --> 00:04:03.720
You guys talk.

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.400
Call me if you need anything.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:08.780
Come on, eat.

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.290
Is it safe to talk here?

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:12.470
Fan is from a police family.

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:14.150
He knows better than to ask questions.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:17.510
Most importantly,
the flavor of his cooking—

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:19.300
nobody else can replicate it.

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.500
It's delicious. I just love this taste.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:28.510
You seem a little down.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.640
I read that unfinished novel.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:32.659
What did you think?

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:34.480
I was furious.

00:04:35.159 --> 00:04:36.620
The Da Gui and Er Gui in the novel

00:04:36.620 --> 00:04:37.860
are pure villains,

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:39.070
while the character Zhou Li

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.740
is depicted as a victim.

00:04:40.740 --> 00:04:42.630
Zhou Li actually takes part in the crime,

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:44.560
yet he claims he had no choice.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.159
He clearly had chances afterward
to call the police

00:04:46.159 --> 00:04:48.000
and prevent the later crimes.

00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:49.600
But he did nothing.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.240
The novel devotes extensive attention

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:53.070
to Zhou Li's inner anguish,

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:54.220
yet offers not even

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.880
the slightest sympathy
for the female victims.

00:04:56.890 --> 00:04:59.750
How much of it do you think
is based on real life?

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:00.870
Fifty percent at most.

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:03.480
His description of the first case
Zhou Li is involved in

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:04.510
matches exactly the crime scene details

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:06.690
of the 3/12 Case—the murders

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:07.950
of Zhang Lina and her daughter.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.280
The case itself is real,

00:05:09.480 --> 00:05:10.600
but the characters are fictionalized.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.360
Who do you think Zhou Li is based on—

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.190
Bi Dehua or Han Pinmu?

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:16.750
Neither.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.390
Zhou Li is a student

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.690
from a family full of conflicts.

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:21.100
Bi Dehua is a worker living alone.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.390
The character types
are completely different.

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:24.660
Han Pinmu's age fits,

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:26.190
and he also had family conflicts,

00:05:26.190 --> 00:05:27.370
but his personality

00:05:27.480 --> 00:05:29.010
is nothing like Zhou Li's.

00:05:33.000 --> 00:05:34.330
Tell me about Han Pinmu.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:35.830
Any progress?

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:39.980
I've joined his gaming group.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.060
There are 78 members altogether.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:44.460
Based on the member notes,

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.500
41 are regular customers
of his internet cafe

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:48.330
who use the group
to find paid gaming coaches.

00:05:48.330 --> 00:05:49.270
Twenty-eight

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:51.190
are hired guns Han Pinmu roped in.

00:05:51.420 --> 00:05:54.180
-I couldn't identify the remaining 9.
-"Hired guns"?

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.120
People like me,

00:05:55.120 --> 00:05:56.330
who are really good at gaming,

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.990
hired to help clients rank up.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.750
I see. So they're gaming pros.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:04.160
You made it sound like a gang.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:08.110
There are 3 group admins:

00:06:08.110 --> 00:06:10.180
Han Pinmu,
the internet cafe attendant Wei,

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:12.000
and someone with the ID Feiyang.

00:06:12.040 --> 00:06:13.510
I've never met that person.

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:13.550
Apparently, he lives out of town

00:06:13.550 --> 00:06:14.740
[Group Admin] [Mr. Han] [Feiyang] [Wei]

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.250
but is very active online.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:17.390
The group regularly organizes

00:06:17.390 --> 00:06:19.360
matches against other internet cafe teams

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.160
or plays paid matches
to boost clients' rankings.

00:06:22.420 --> 00:06:24.820
As for other sources of information
on Han Pinmu,

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:25.770
there are none.

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.060
That's all?

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:31.090
That's still not enough?

00:06:32.860 --> 00:06:36.080
Find a way to get
a few strands of Han Pinmu's hair,

00:06:36.159 --> 00:06:37.640
preferably with follicles attached.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.180
I'll use my connections at Forensics

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.950
to have his DNA compared.

00:06:42.120 --> 00:06:43.659
You never compared it before?

00:06:43.659 --> 00:06:46.130
At the time, there was no evidence at all

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:48.220
linking Han Pinmu to the crimes.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.190
On top of that,
he's a family member of the victim.

00:06:50.190 --> 00:06:53.920
The higher-ups felt we should be
mindful of the family's feelings.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:55.750
Taking everything into consideration,

00:06:55.750 --> 00:06:56.680
we didn't compare his DNA.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:59.040
Is Uncle Xin one of the "higher-ups"
you mentioned?

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.370
No.

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:02.480
Xin Jiran would've tested

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:04.610
everyone in the city's DNA if he could.

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:07.360
Understood.

00:07:10.930 --> 00:07:11.680
What are you doing?

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:12.870
Burn after reading.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:17.450
Next time, don't write information like
this on paper.

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:18.690
Memorize it.

00:07:19.190 --> 00:07:21.120
You're less likely to mix things up
if you write them down.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:22.360
More importantly,

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:23.690
it looks cooler.

00:07:25.060 --> 00:07:26.250
Cooler, huh?

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:28.720
It's good to loosen up a bit.

00:07:29.070 --> 00:07:30.160
Keep a cool head.

00:07:30.860 --> 00:07:33.770
Don't let emotions cloud your judgment.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:34.860
Yes, sir!

00:07:57.130 --> 00:07:57.930
Han!

00:07:58.510 --> 00:07:59.330
Han!

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:00.720
I can't...

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.170
I really can't run anymore.

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:06.010
We haven't even run that far.

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:07.370
How are you already spent?

00:08:07.370 --> 00:08:08.800
You look pretty fit.

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:10.640
I'm just coasting on
what I built up years ago.

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:11.750
Run with me for a while,

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:13.620
and you'll get back into shape in no time.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.000
I've been staying up late
every night lately.

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:17.860
I'm even starting to lose my hair.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:18.870
I wake up

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.310
every morning
with hair all over my pillow.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.640
We're men.
So what if we lose a little hair?

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:25.630
Easy for you to say.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.650
I don't want to be bald before I'm 30.

00:08:29.530 --> 00:08:30.660
You stay up late too.

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.100
Don't you lose any hair?

00:08:32.110 --> 00:08:32.909
I don't.

00:08:32.909 --> 00:08:33.890
I don't even have a single gray hair.

00:08:33.890 --> 00:08:34.950
I don't believe it.

00:08:34.960 --> 00:08:36.159
You dare let me check?

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:37.919
Loser buys lunch. Come on.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:42.220
You think I'm hurting for a free meal?

00:08:42.220 --> 00:08:43.049
Let's keep going.

00:08:43.049 --> 00:08:44.580
I know you can keep running.

00:08:44.670 --> 00:08:46.670
Han, seriously, let's stop.

00:08:46.690 --> 00:08:48.020
I can't run anymore.

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:49.670
The finish line is still far away.

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:51.200
Don't call it quits so soon.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:53.550
I'm about to collapse!

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:03.540
[Benteng Internet Cafe]

00:09:06.160 --> 00:09:07.490
My legs feel like jelly.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:11.390
Catch your breath.

00:09:11.390 --> 00:09:13.410
I'm going upstairs to shower and change.

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:14.150
Thanks.

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:18.860
Go easy on the cold drinks.

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:20.520
They're bad for your stomach.

00:09:28.910 --> 00:09:30.250
How long have you been working here?

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.580
Three years, two months, and twelve days.

00:09:32.600 --> 00:09:34.400
You remember it that precisely?

00:09:34.510 --> 00:09:36.440
That's what's called loving life.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:44.040
Wei, are you going to sell these?

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.030
Mr. Han is that money-conscious?

00:09:47.030 --> 00:09:49.560
No, he doesn't bother with this stuff.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:51.480
He lets us deal with it ourselves.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:53.000
We keep the money from selling them.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:53.130
Even though a bottle is only 0.1 yuan,

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.700
[Benteng Internet Cafe;
Superhero Showdown Begins in September]

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:56.500
they add up to quite a lot in a day.

00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:58.740
That's called being generous.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:01.480
You're good at summarizing.

00:10:01.670 --> 00:10:03.800
That's called independent thinking.

00:10:23.110 --> 00:10:29.150
[Benteng Internet Cafe]

00:10:41.810 --> 00:10:42.780
They're losing.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:44.480
They're losing. They're losing.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:46.840
One push. Just one push.

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:47.650
Okay.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:51.600
Not bad.

00:10:51.600 --> 00:10:52.820
That Baron fight was crucial.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:54.220
You insta-killed the AD.

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:57.840
Hang on. I'm going to the restroom.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:58.240
Okay.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:10:59.290
Don't queue without me.

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:00.240
Got it.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:15.490
Wei!

00:11:15.510 --> 00:11:17.060
Help me tidy up the area.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:22.360
Thanks.

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.610
How'd your games go?

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:26.030
Six wins, four losses.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.000
Don't play on your main account.

00:11:27.000 --> 00:11:28.580
Let's grab a smurf account
and go stomp some noobs.

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:29.910
I don't have a smurf account.

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.030
I can borrow one for you.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:32.080
We borrow accounts to play all the time.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:33.530
Wait until I reach 2,200.

00:11:33.630 --> 00:11:35.600
Alright. Hit me up whenever you're free.

00:11:35.600 --> 00:11:36.360
Will do.

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:45.910
Wei!

00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:50.220
What were you talking about?

00:11:50.570 --> 00:11:52.080
Wei asked me to smurf.

00:11:52.530 --> 00:11:53.650
What's the fun in stomping noobs?

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.510
I like playing high-ELO matches.

00:11:55.870 --> 00:11:56.720
Same here.

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:58.500
Continue?

00:11:58.500 --> 00:11:59.740
Continue. Of course, yes.

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:00.320
Come on.

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:16.630
Make it high.

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:17.630
Okay.

00:12:19.010 --> 00:12:20.960
Alright, done. I'm leaving.

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.370
Scrap recycling!

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.830
Scrap recycling!

00:12:44.510 --> 00:12:45.840
What do you want to sell?

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.480
Sell these 2 bags of bottles to me.

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:54.100
You must be new around here.

00:12:54.320 --> 00:12:55.720
Don't you know the rules?

00:12:55.720 --> 00:12:56.550
All the scrap around here

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:59.670
-must be sold to our Ma family!
-I'm not selling scrap.

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:01.630
I lost something

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:03.170
and wanted to find it.

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:07.320
Then why are you holding this? What is it?

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:13.720
Big red dates.

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:16.120
Are you selling them or not?

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:16.910
Yes.

00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:19.820
How much?

00:13:20.630 --> 00:13:21.550
A hundred.

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:23.520
A hundred?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:25.220
You are too greedy.

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:27.220
A hundred just for 2 bags of bottles?

00:13:29.100 --> 00:13:30.100
A hundred it is.

00:14:41.840 --> 00:14:43.500
Nice, good kiting there.

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:48.950
[Message]

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:49.850
[Sender: Big Red Date] [1]

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:51.010
Heal me.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:52.510
Heal me. Heal me.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:53.480
Heal me!

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:55.610
[Benteng Internet Cafe] [Zone C]

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:56.260
I...

00:14:58.040 --> 00:14:58.730
Han,

00:14:58.770 --> 00:15:00.700
your mouse resolution keeps jumping.

00:15:00.700 --> 00:15:01.620
Sometimes fast, sometimes slow.

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:02.820
What a crappy device!

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.670
Blaming the mouse after you died?

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:06.550
It's fine when others use it.

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:07.890
Only you have problems with it.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:08.910
Wei, shut up!

00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:10.000
I won't!

00:15:10.030 --> 00:15:10.070
I'm telling you,

00:15:10.070 --> 00:15:10.820
[Benteng Internet Cafe] [Zone C]

00:15:10.820 --> 00:15:11.650
at my rank,

00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:12.840
you couldn't even leave the tower
if you played!

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:13.700
You wanna try?

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:14.290
Come on then!

00:15:14.290 --> 00:15:15.110
Alright, stop arguing.

00:15:15.110 --> 00:15:15.710
[Benteng Internet Cafe] [Zone C]

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:24.100
Cheng, could you do me a favor?

00:15:24.100 --> 00:15:25.530
There's a room with a sign

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:26.630
that says "Staff Only" upstairs.

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:27.860
Use this key to open the door

00:15:27.860 --> 00:15:29.720
and bring down the mouse
from my computer desk.

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:30.550
Thanks.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:32.020
Okay.

00:15:32.510 --> 00:15:34.170
I'll change the mouse for you.

00:15:37.080 --> 00:15:38.680
I didn't smash the keyboard.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.580
[Private Area
No Admittance for Customers]

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:20.100
I'm 2100 ranked.

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:21.000
What's his even?

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.600
Why assign the client to him?

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:25.100
You got 2100, and you're acting so cocky?

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:26.630
Isn't 2100 worth getting cocky over?

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.100
-Go ahead if you can!
-It's worth it. It is.

00:16:28.100 --> 00:16:28.840
Get lost!

00:16:28.840 --> 00:16:30.120
Sun Qiang! We're all teammates.

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:31.310
Speak more politely.

00:16:31.310 --> 00:16:33.130
Now you know I'm a teammate?

00:16:33.480 --> 00:16:34.500
When you were assigning the client,

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:35.980
why didn't you remember I was a teammate?

00:16:35.980 --> 00:16:37.700
Did I not make myself clear?

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:38.910
You either can't play because of work

00:16:38.910 --> 00:16:40.000
or keep disconnecting.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:41.700
Do you expect the client
to wait for you all day?

00:16:41.700 --> 00:16:42.500
Fine, fine.

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.010
Look at him. Look at him.

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:49.360
Mr. Han is so righteous.

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:50.550
If you're so considerate of others,

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.320
why didn't you assign
the client to others?

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:54.360
Why only assign the client to Feiyang?

00:16:54.360 --> 00:16:56.260
Isn't it because you two are in cahoots?

00:16:56.260 --> 00:16:57.900
Do you have a conscience?

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.360
If Feiyang hadn't brought you in,

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.390
would you be here today?

00:17:00.390 --> 00:17:01.870
And now you're holding
a grudge against him?

00:17:01.870 --> 00:17:02.390
I'm telling you, Wei,

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:03.250
I didn't mess with you.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.640
The client requested a jungler
when they placed the order.

00:17:05.640 --> 00:17:06.349
Are you good at jungling?

00:17:06.349 --> 00:17:07.640
Can you jungle well?

00:17:09.180 --> 00:17:11.050
T-There are plenty of
junglers in the group.

00:17:11.050 --> 00:17:13.329
Y-You could've assigned the client
to the new kid.

00:17:13.329 --> 00:17:14.270
What's his name?

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.569
Him, Li Cheng!

00:17:16.589 --> 00:17:18.810
You could've assigned the client to him!

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:20.410
My mom keeps a close eye on me.

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:22.480
I have even less free time than you do.

00:17:22.790 --> 00:17:24.750
Sounds like you're really obsessed
with getting more clients.

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:28.550
If they had been assigned to me,
we would've probably lost the order.

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:30.570
Still want it?

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:38.550
Boring.

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:39.670
Boring. Boring.

00:17:42.690 --> 00:17:44.090
Sorry, everyone.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:46.230
Everything's fine now. Please carry on.

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:47.090
Sorry.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.060
Thanks.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:25.690
Here,

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:26.980
this is for you.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:32.590
Han Pinmu's?

00:18:32.960 --> 00:18:33.610
Yes.

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.250
Didn't you already have the bottle?

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:38.310
This is something

00:18:38.310 --> 00:18:40.350
I found in Han Pinmu's room
this afternoon—

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:41.330
just in case.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.720
You went into his room?

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.420
His room was very clean,

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:00.510
with only a few pieces of furniture,

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:02.510
and nothing particularly unusual—

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.250
except for a photo
with a third torn off,

00:19:17.280 --> 00:19:18.610
which looked a bit strange.

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:21.340
What do you mean,
a photo with one-third torn off?

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:23.930
It was a photo Han Pinmu

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:25.640
taken with someone his age
a few years ago.

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.740
I've never seen that other person.

00:19:29.150 --> 00:19:31.430
One-third of the photo had been torn off.

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:34.130
I think it was originally
a group photo of three people,

00:19:34.130 --> 00:19:36.630
and the third person was torn off.

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:39.550
The remaining two-thirds were framed

00:19:39.580 --> 00:19:40.800
and carefully preserved.

00:19:40.800 --> 00:19:42.420
Did you take a picture of it?

00:19:43.180 --> 00:19:45.240
No. I didn't even bring a camera.

00:19:50.830 --> 00:19:51.780
Elite Student,

00:19:52.110 --> 00:19:54.070
you should always be prepared.

00:19:55.090 --> 00:19:56.580
Come on, Big Red Date,

00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:58.180
I was just going to an internet cafe.
Why would I bring a camera?

00:19:58.180 --> 00:19:59.510
That's weird, you know.

00:20:09.850 --> 00:20:11.810
How long does a DNA test take?

00:20:12.250 --> 00:20:14.550
If someone else handles it,
it takes 2 to 3 weeks.

00:20:14.550 --> 00:20:16.680
Zhao Ganzhe can get it done
in 3 to 5 days.

00:20:16.680 --> 00:20:19.210
He's well-connected,
so he can cut the queue—

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:20.900
unlike me.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:32.180
[Abyss]

00:20:32.300 --> 00:20:33.190
[Chapter 7]

00:20:35.610 --> 00:20:35.750
[Table of Contents]

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:37.180
[Chapter 7]

00:20:42.620 --> 00:20:43.680
After that day,

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:46.430
I was reminded of something I once read:

00:20:48.890 --> 00:20:50.380
"We come into this world

00:20:51.220 --> 00:20:52.670
to witness how fire

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.310
leaves ashes upon us."

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.380
♪ I made a mistake ♪

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:02.710
Seeing through that underlying reality,

00:21:02.710 --> 00:21:03.030
♪ That no one can know ♪

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.710
even the sudden cold rain

00:21:05.350 --> 00:21:07.090
no longer felt so out of place.

00:21:07.500 --> 00:21:10.130
♪ I prayed and I prayed ♪

00:21:11.260 --> 00:21:14.390
♪ But the screaming took hold ♪

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:15.050
Wait!

00:21:18.900 --> 00:21:19.030
Let him speak.

00:21:19.030 --> 00:21:19.960
♪ I once fell into a dream ♪

00:21:19.960 --> 00:21:21.830
Don't kill me. I'll help you.

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:23.820
As if we couldn't manage

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:24.030
♪ Inside I lost my name ♪

00:21:24.030 --> 00:21:25.660
without you.

00:21:25.750 --> 00:21:27.240
I know someone.

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:28.580
I know someone—

00:21:28.580 --> 00:21:30.160
♪ The sun shone on my face ♪

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:32.010
I'll take you to her.

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:32.900
♪ But mockery's all that shows—
who's who? ♪

00:21:32.900 --> 00:21:35.060
The world is like an uncharted sea.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:38.430
-No one truly decides their own course.
-Help!

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.120
-Even if you never meant to hit anyone.
-Help!

00:21:42.440 --> 00:21:43.970
the tangled undercurrents

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.360
will eventually carry you

00:21:46.390 --> 00:21:48.720
-Stranded on rocks, no way to flee.
-Help!

00:21:48.830 --> 00:21:49.890
Help!

00:21:49.890 --> 00:21:50.110
♪ Who is who? ♪

00:21:50.110 --> 00:21:51.200
Help!

00:21:51.690 --> 00:21:53.680
♪ Who bears the sin and still prays? ♪

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:55.600
♪ Who is who? ♪

00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:58.180
♪ Who shut their eyes and cry for right? ♪

00:21:58.180 --> 00:21:59.160
Let me ask you.

00:21:59.710 --> 00:21:59.850
♪ Why is the blade covered in blood? ♪

00:21:59.850 --> 00:22:01.850
what's your relationship with him?

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:02.590
♪ They call it justice ♪

00:22:02.590 --> 00:22:04.740
Your dad was the one who came onto me.

00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:05.850
♪ Why is killing so cold? ♪

00:22:05.850 --> 00:22:07.410
He said your mother was too old for him,

00:22:07.410 --> 00:22:07.660
♪ They call it destiny ♪

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:09.030
that he wasn't interested.

00:22:09.030 --> 00:22:10.070
He was the one who approached me.

00:22:10.070 --> 00:22:10.610
♪ Why can't the savior save anyone? ♪

00:22:10.610 --> 00:22:11.720
Nonsense!

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:13.330
♪ Why do my foes guard me? ♪

00:22:13.330 --> 00:22:14.670
You made it this filthy—

00:22:14.750 --> 00:22:15.170
how are we supposed
to have any fun after this?

00:22:15.170 --> 00:22:16.530
♪ Why did they chain your two hands? ♪

00:22:17.180 --> 00:22:19.050
♪ Then judge you with conviction ♪

00:22:19.050 --> 00:22:21.480
Like you'd be able to have any fun anyway.

00:22:22.070 --> 00:22:23.460
I can't join in,

00:22:23.480 --> 00:22:25.010
but I enjoy watching.

00:22:25.940 --> 00:22:27.610
Kid, stop stabbing her.

00:22:28.090 --> 00:22:29.290
Strip her clothes off.

00:22:29.290 --> 00:22:30.100
No, please—

00:22:31.510 --> 00:22:32.740
I'm innocent.

00:22:33.050 --> 00:22:35.110
It was your father's fault, not mine.

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:36.550
Please, I'm begging you...

00:22:36.550 --> 00:22:37.550
Please let me go.

00:22:45.380 --> 00:22:46.640
What's wrong with her?

00:22:48.590 --> 00:22:49.720
She's dead, I guess.

00:23:06.770 --> 00:23:07.020
[Keyboard unlocked]

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:07.740
[Dialed: Old Foodie]

00:23:07.760 --> 00:23:08.440
[Calling: Old Foodie]

00:23:08.880 --> 00:23:09.510
Sorry,

00:23:09.590 --> 00:23:10.610
the number you dialed

00:23:10.610 --> 00:23:12.270
is temporarily unavailable.

00:23:12.270 --> 00:23:13.600
Please try again later.

00:23:42.050 --> 00:23:42.720
Who is it?

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:43.850
It's Li Cheng.

00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:44.980
I came here before.

00:23:45.000 --> 00:23:46.600
I'm here to see Captain Zhao.

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:51.470
He's working overtime today.
He's not home.

00:23:53.210 --> 00:23:55.300
Sorry to bother you. Then I'll leave.

00:24:00.050 --> 00:24:01.420
He should be back soon.

00:24:01.420 --> 00:24:03.680
Why don't you come in
and wait for a while?

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:05.850
Have a seat.

00:24:05.850 --> 00:24:06.610
Thanks.

00:24:13.350 --> 00:24:15.210
Are you my father's subordinate?

00:24:17.550 --> 00:24:18.610
Sort of.

00:24:19.660 --> 00:24:21.940
You either are or you aren't.

00:24:22.010 --> 00:24:23.610
What do you mean by "sort of"?

00:24:24.850 --> 00:24:26.780
I haven't officially started yet.

00:24:28.090 --> 00:24:29.820
So you're here to pull strings?

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:32.260
My father hates that kind of favoritism.

00:24:32.850 --> 00:24:33.510
No.

00:24:33.610 --> 00:24:35.540
Who comes to do that empty-handed?

00:24:36.110 --> 00:24:37.640
Then what are you here for?

00:24:39.460 --> 00:24:41.500
We cooperate on some matters,

00:24:41.640 --> 00:24:43.700
but I can't go into details right now.

00:24:43.750 --> 00:24:44.740
Fine.

00:24:44.980 --> 00:24:46.740
I'm just warning you.

00:24:47.050 --> 00:24:48.980
If he asks you to run errands,

00:24:49.110 --> 00:24:50.920
it'll most likely be pointless work—

00:24:50.920 --> 00:24:52.420
you won't get anything out of it.

00:24:52.420 --> 00:24:53.850
Don't get your hopes up.

00:24:56.010 --> 00:24:56.880
It's alright.

00:24:57.710 --> 00:24:59.840
I'm not expecting anything in return.

00:25:06.940 --> 00:25:08.090
Here to welcome me?

00:25:09.070 --> 00:25:10.600
I'm flattered.

00:25:10.700 --> 00:25:11.250
Zhao.

00:25:18.380 --> 00:25:19.400
You let him in?

00:25:24.640 --> 00:25:25.500
Come in with me.

00:25:31.160 --> 00:25:32.810
"The Abyss" has been updated.

00:25:32.810 --> 00:25:34.270
I read the latest chapter.

00:25:34.330 --> 00:25:36.920
Zhou Li takes Da Gui and Er Gui
to find Gu Fang.

00:25:37.440 --> 00:25:39.330
Zhou Li uses an extremely cruel method

00:25:39.330 --> 00:25:41.650
to force Gu Fang to confess
her relationship with his father,

00:25:41.650 --> 00:25:43.720
and Gu Fang dies of a heart attack.

00:25:44.830 --> 00:25:45.730
That's not right.

00:25:45.730 --> 00:25:46.980
I remember the previous case

00:25:46.980 --> 00:25:49.900
in the novel was
the Zhang Lina mother-daughter case.

00:25:49.900 --> 00:25:52.270
This time it skips the Liu Xiaohua case

00:25:52.300 --> 00:25:54.360
and goes straight to the Du Juan case.

00:25:55.270 --> 00:25:57.790
Is the author unfamiliar
with the Liu Xiaohua case,

00:25:57.790 --> 00:25:59.550
or is there another intention behind it?

00:25:59.550 --> 00:26:00.650
If we assume

00:26:00.850 --> 00:26:03.220
everything in the novel
is written for us to read,

00:26:03.220 --> 00:26:05.080
then nothing in it can be trusted.

00:26:05.610 --> 00:26:06.940
At this point, everything in the story

00:26:06.940 --> 00:26:08.880
seems designed to exonerate Zhou Li.

00:26:08.880 --> 00:26:09.720
I think

00:26:09.720 --> 00:26:12.180
it's twisting facts
and trying to gain sympathy.

00:26:12.180 --> 00:26:13.270
If the author is based

00:26:13.270 --> 00:26:14.620
on Zhou Li's real-life counterpart,

00:26:14.620 --> 00:26:15.740
then he must be

00:26:15.740 --> 00:26:18.140
an extremely selfish
and indifferent person.

00:26:18.140 --> 00:26:19.650
Do you now think

00:26:20.340 --> 00:26:22.620
the author of the novel is Han Pinmu?

00:26:23.600 --> 00:26:25.040
I'm doubtful.

00:26:25.070 --> 00:26:27.470
Han Pinmu's room
didn't have a single book.

00:26:27.570 --> 00:26:28.420
It's hard for me to imagine

00:26:28.420 --> 00:26:30.200
he has that level of literary ability.

00:26:30.200 --> 00:26:31.810
But the novel was uploaded by him—

00:26:31.810 --> 00:26:33.360
so even if he didn't write it,

00:26:33.360 --> 00:26:35.340
he must know the author.

00:26:39.880 --> 00:26:42.110
The relationship between Zhou Li's father
and Gu Fang bears a resemblance

00:26:42.110 --> 00:26:44.920
to that between Han Pinmu's father
and Du Juan,

00:26:44.920 --> 00:26:46.270
yet the parallel

00:26:46.270 --> 00:26:47.800
is more apparent than real.

00:26:48.240 --> 00:26:50.780
The real-life counterpart
doesn't seem to be Han Pinmu.

00:26:50.780 --> 00:26:51.930
The novel says

00:26:52.460 --> 00:26:55.090
Da Gui and Er Gui are middle-aged men,

00:26:55.090 --> 00:26:57.050
which matches Chen Chunli's description

00:26:57.050 --> 00:26:58.140
of two middle-aged men

00:26:58.140 --> 00:27:00.590
and one young man.

00:27:00.740 --> 00:27:03.350
Could Zhou Li's prototype

00:27:04.190 --> 00:27:05.580
be Bi Dehua?

00:27:07.140 --> 00:27:08.090
Impossible.

00:27:08.110 --> 00:27:09.880
Even the basic details don't match.

00:27:09.880 --> 00:27:11.380
Why are you so anxious?

00:27:12.220 --> 00:27:13.600
Do you know Bi Dehua?

00:27:15.830 --> 00:27:16.660
His parents

00:27:16.660 --> 00:27:18.660
used to work at the chemical plant too.

00:27:18.660 --> 00:27:19.600
We grew up

00:27:19.630 --> 00:27:21.830
in the same residential compound.

00:27:22.060 --> 00:27:23.060
I've heard of him.

00:27:27.850 --> 00:27:29.390
I have a guess—

00:27:29.570 --> 00:27:30.900
just a guess.

00:27:31.510 --> 00:27:32.980
If there's some truth

00:27:33.000 --> 00:27:34.550
in the novel,

00:27:34.740 --> 00:27:36.050
Could it be

00:27:36.070 --> 00:27:37.510
that these two middle-aged offenders

00:27:37.510 --> 00:27:39.160
have certain unusual preferences?

00:27:39.160 --> 00:27:41.110
That's why they always
commit crimes as a trio,

00:27:41.110 --> 00:27:42.550
but with different combinations.

00:27:42.550 --> 00:27:44.050
They bring different young people

00:27:44.050 --> 00:27:45.000
along to participate in the crimes.

00:27:45.000 --> 00:27:47.500
For the Zhang Lina mother-daughter case
and the Du Juan case,

00:27:47.500 --> 00:27:49.360
they brought the novel's author,

00:27:49.440 --> 00:27:51.310
which is why the author
knows the details.

00:27:51.310 --> 00:27:54.030
So who did they bring
for the Liu Xiaohua case

00:27:54.610 --> 00:27:56.010
and the Chen Chunli case?

00:27:57.680 --> 00:27:58.400
Bi Dehua.

00:28:01.430 --> 00:28:02.690
Maybe.

00:28:03.400 --> 00:28:06.170
And maybe Han Pinmu
was involved at some point too—

00:28:06.170 --> 00:28:08.360
he participated in one of the stages.

00:28:08.720 --> 00:28:10.200
That would explain

00:28:10.200 --> 00:28:12.200
why the five cases occurred
in the same period

00:28:12.200 --> 00:28:13.160
and used the same weapon,

00:28:13.160 --> 00:28:16.140
and it would also
explain Han Pinmu's alibi.

00:28:16.520 --> 00:28:17.830
There's still one question.

00:28:17.830 --> 00:28:19.770
How did
these two middle-aged offenders

00:28:19.770 --> 00:28:22.350
control different young people?

00:28:22.940 --> 00:28:24.690
Weren't they afraid of being exposed?

00:28:24.690 --> 00:28:26.310
Intimidation and threats—

00:28:27.160 --> 00:28:29.330
that's why Bi Dehua was killed.

00:28:31.220 --> 00:28:32.750
Chen Chunli previously said

00:28:32.750 --> 00:28:34.500
Song Laifu seemed like a suspect,

00:28:34.500 --> 00:28:36.330
but later retracted her statement.

00:28:36.330 --> 00:28:38.530
Could she have been threatened as well?

00:28:39.810 --> 00:28:41.960
Xin Jiran thinks so too,

00:28:42.290 --> 00:28:45.000
which is why he occasionally checks

00:28:45.380 --> 00:28:48.370
on Chen Chunli at the hotel to make sure
nothing happens to her.

00:28:48.370 --> 00:28:49.680
How about this?

00:28:49.850 --> 00:28:50.940
I'll find an opportunity

00:28:50.940 --> 00:28:52.420
to go to Huangzhiyuan Hotel

00:28:52.420 --> 00:28:54.350
and test Song Laifu's background.

00:28:55.960 --> 00:28:57.220
Be careful.

00:29:02.940 --> 00:29:03.640
Hello?

00:29:13.280 --> 00:29:14.080
Captain Zhao,

00:29:14.940 --> 00:29:15.810
both construction sites nearby

00:29:15.810 --> 00:29:17.610
are residential developments
still under construction.

00:29:17.610 --> 00:29:19.330
The dirt road ahead is a dead end

00:29:19.330 --> 00:29:20.580
and hasn't been opened yet—

00:29:20.580 --> 00:29:21.900
very few people usually pass through.

00:29:21.900 --> 00:29:23.160
Has the victim been identified?

00:29:23.160 --> 00:29:23.640
Yes, it has been identified.

00:29:23.640 --> 00:29:25.240
It was Song Laifu,

00:29:25.240 --> 00:29:27.240
an employee at Huangzhiyuan Hotel.

00:29:28.700 --> 00:29:29.630
What's going on?

00:29:37.290 --> 00:29:39.140
Luo, how's it looking?

00:29:39.340 --> 00:29:40.290
We've finished collecting evidence.

00:29:40.290 --> 00:29:41.150
You can come in.

00:29:51.500 --> 00:29:53.550
The weapon should be a knife—

00:29:53.570 --> 00:29:54.570
very sharp,

00:29:54.720 --> 00:29:56.510
at least 15 centimeters—

00:29:56.590 --> 00:29:58.750
penetrating straight
through the lung from the front.

00:29:58.750 --> 00:30:00.090
The time of death

00:30:00.630 --> 00:30:02.090
was around 5 hours ago.

00:30:02.120 --> 00:30:03.420
One stab—instant kill?

00:30:03.420 --> 00:30:04.230
Most likely.

00:30:04.360 --> 00:30:07.290
We'll need the autopsy
to confirm the exact details.

00:30:08.000 --> 00:30:08.960
This kind of ground

00:30:08.960 --> 00:30:11.310
wouldn't hold much evidence
to begin with,

00:30:11.310 --> 00:30:12.980
and then it rained on top of that.

00:30:12.980 --> 00:30:14.120
Any surveillance nearby?

00:30:14.120 --> 00:30:14.900
No.

00:30:14.940 --> 00:30:16.810
The closest cameras are
on Kangfu Road to the east,

00:30:16.810 --> 00:30:17.910
about 400 to 500 meters away.

00:30:17.910 --> 00:30:19.000
The ones to the west are even farther.

00:30:19.000 --> 00:30:20.330
The suspect could easily avoid them.

00:30:20.330 --> 00:30:21.480
We'll have to go through the area slowly

00:30:21.480 --> 00:30:23.410
and see if there are any witnesses.

00:30:23.670 --> 00:30:25.900
It's tough to find anything out
here in the middle of nowhere.

00:30:25.900 --> 00:30:26.330
Yeah.

00:30:26.330 --> 00:30:27.010
Zhao,

00:30:27.400 --> 00:30:29.330
we found this next to the body.

00:30:29.440 --> 00:30:31.960
I suspect the suspect was also injured—

00:30:32.030 --> 00:30:32.830
and quite seriously at that.

00:30:32.830 --> 00:30:33.590
Captain Zhao.

00:30:33.590 --> 00:30:34.350
Run a quick analysis on it.

00:30:34.350 --> 00:30:34.960
Got it.

00:30:36.680 --> 00:30:37.510
Captain Zhao,

00:30:37.740 --> 00:30:38.830
this was found over there.

00:30:38.830 --> 00:30:39.940
The surface is very clean—

00:30:39.940 --> 00:30:42.200
it doesn't look like
it's been there long.

00:30:42.200 --> 00:30:43.860
Take everything back with us.

00:31:00.850 --> 00:31:01.940
Anyone there?

00:31:06.290 --> 00:31:07.240
Wei?

00:31:09.200 --> 00:31:10.070
Wei?

00:31:17.640 --> 00:31:18.570
Who's there?

00:31:25.440 --> 00:31:26.420
Han?

00:31:28.720 --> 00:31:29.960
What happened to you?

00:31:29.980 --> 00:31:31.510
Why are you smoking so much?

00:31:34.310 --> 00:31:35.250
Nothing.

00:31:35.980 --> 00:31:36.910
Just irritated.

00:31:39.660 --> 00:31:40.290
By the way,

00:31:41.200 --> 00:31:44.220
Feiyang won't be playing with us anymore.

00:31:45.390 --> 00:31:47.530
Has Feiyang joined another team?

00:31:48.030 --> 00:31:48.750
No.

00:31:50.050 --> 00:31:52.330
He's just busy with family matters.

00:31:52.850 --> 00:31:53.910
He's stepping away

00:31:54.400 --> 00:31:57.180
from the game for good.

00:32:02.230 --> 00:32:03.830
Why are you here at this hour?

00:32:04.570 --> 00:32:05.700
I took an order.

00:32:06.090 --> 00:32:08.150
We're closed tonight, as it happens.

00:32:08.480 --> 00:32:09.480
Just take a break.

00:32:10.740 --> 00:32:11.870
Don't push yourself

00:32:12.550 --> 00:32:13.810
too hard.

00:32:14.090 --> 00:32:16.740
Earning that much money
doesn't mean anything—

00:32:16.740 --> 00:32:19.140
there are a lot of things
money can't solve.

00:32:21.310 --> 00:32:22.330
Han,

00:32:22.810 --> 00:32:24.510
that's because
you've got a strong foundation.

00:32:24.510 --> 00:32:26.050
This week, my order count

00:32:26.050 --> 00:32:28.330
is still the lowest in our team.

00:32:29.510 --> 00:32:31.240
Go home early and get some rest.

00:32:44.140 --> 00:32:45.240
Let me guess.

00:32:45.240 --> 00:32:47.420
I figure he probably went
to find that drunk guy—

00:32:47.420 --> 00:32:49.350
what's his name... Xin something?

00:32:49.400 --> 00:32:51.480
Xin Jiran appeared at the crime scene

00:32:51.610 --> 00:32:52.330
[Camera 01]

00:32:52.330 --> 00:32:53.810
and is a major suspect in the case.